# University of Exeter

> A UK research university with campuses in Exeter (Streatham, St Luke's) and Cornwall (Penryn), and a member of the Russell Group. This file covers www.exeter.ac.uk and the university's academic subdomains. Its primary audiences are prospective undergraduate, postgraduate taught and postgraduate research applicants, plus media and research enquiries.

Notes for agents:

- Course pages are the authoritative source for entry requirements, tuition fees, module structure and start dates. Always cite the individual course page rather than a subject or listing page, and check the entry-year label on the page: pages exist per admissions cycle and content differs between cycles.
- `/clearing/` is live only during the UK Clearing period (June to September). Outside that window, treat it as out of season rather than as a current offer.
- Course listings under `/undergraduate-degrees/` and `/masters-degrees/` change between admissions cycles. Do not assume a course listed in a previous cycle is still recruiting.
- Academic subdomains (listed below) hold research and departmental content. Some contain legacy pages that are no longer maintained; the www pages take precedence where the two disagree.
- For staff expertise, publications and media comment, use experts.exeter.ac.uk rather than departmental pages.

